enemies.bossShark.lunge.range,22,4,40,"bossShark lunge: gap (units) inside which it may commit to a run"
enemies.bossShark.lunge.minRange,11,1,20,"bossShark lunge: closer than this there is no wind-up worth watching, so it does not start one"
enemies.bossShark.lunge.windup,1.3,0.1,3,"bossShark lunge: seconds of the tell - throttled, turning onto you, jaw opening, ring drawing in"
enemies.bossShark.lunge.windSpeedMul,0.25,0.05,1,"bossShark lunge: cruise x this while it gathers (and between the runs of a double or a feint)"
enemies.bossShark.lunge.speedMul,3.8,1,6,"bossShark lunge: cruise x this down the locked line"
enemies.bossShark.lunge.strikeTime,1.2,0.1,3,"bossShark lunge: seconds the run stays committed; range/speedMul/strikeTime are read together - the run should cross where you were and blow past"
enemies.bossShark.lunge.strikeTurnRate,0.15,0,3,"bossShark lunge: rad/s of correction mid-run - enough to punish standing still, never enough to follow a seal that moved"
enemies.bossShark.lunge.cooldown,5.5,0.5,30,"bossShark lunge: seconds after a run recovers before it may commit another. Cut from 8.5 because one perk on a five-to-sixteen-second cooldown plus a bite was the whole of a boss's aggression, and a full cycle here - wind-up, strike, rest - was eleven seconds, so a boss committed to something about eight times in a fight and chipped you the rest of it. npm run test:bossthreat prints the cadence."
enemies.bossShark.lunge.damageMul,4,1,8,"bossShark lunge: what the run multiplies its contact damage by while it is travelling. The number that was missing. A committed pass is billed as an ATTACK now rather than as chip (see isCommittedRun in entities/enemies.js and the contact call in systems/combat.js) - before that it drew on CONFIG.boss.damageCap.contactPerSecond, a seventh of the bar a second, which made the most telegraphed thing a boss does worth exactly as much as drifting into its tail fin. Promoting the channel alone would only have moved the ceiling; this is what reaches it. Read against the kraken crush (2.5 on a 0.9s wind-up) and the lunge perk (2): those two multiply a body that was already billed as an attack, and this one has a longer tell than either. THE FOUR NUMBERS DIFFER BECAUSE THE BODIES DO, and that is the whole reason this is not one shared constant. Contact is a per-SECOND drain, so what a pass is worth is how long the seal is inside the animal - a chord through its body at lunge speed - and the hammerhead's radius is 1.3 against the shark's 2.2, so at a shared multiplier its pass was worth less than half. At these four a connecting lunge is 18-27% of a fresh seal bar at the opening boss, which is the spread npm run test:bossthreat prints and gates. Late in a run every one of them is against CONFIG.boss.damageCap.perSecond instead, so a boss can take three quarters of your health in one pass and - by that same cap - can never take all of it. That is the intent: it is the thing you are meant to move out of the way of."
